This invariant can be used to easily check if a circuit polynomial is nonnegative, see \cite[Theorem 1.1]{iliman2016amoebas}. Let $f$ be a circuit polynomial as in~\eqref{eq:defcircuit}, then $f$ is nonnegative if and only if 
 $f$ is a sum of monomial squares, or
