starting point $1$ at typical points $x\in\mathbb{R}$.
We say that a point $x\in\mathbb{R}$ is a \emph{point of slow growth}
for \eqref{u} if $|u(t\,,x)-1|=\mathcal{O}(t^{1/4})$ as $t\to0^+$
a.s. 
